                    {
                        "name":  "places/ChIJW_lv_hmpQjQRFslAyToEpRE/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnTUN3X3NiM2xBRRAB",
                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "a year ago",
                        "rating":  5,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "Pataya Fried Rice ($295):\nIt’s their chef’s special fried rice and the taste actually hits different with a mixture of saltiness, umami, slight spiciness. The fried rice is well seasoned with various spices and covers some squid inside.\n\nMilk Tea (Teh Tarik) ($130) (Cold/Hot):\nThe origin of this milk tea can be traced back to Indian-Muslim immigrants in the Malay Peninsula. In my opinion, not going to lie this is one of the best milk tea I’ve ever had, which tastes sweeter and creamier than Taiwanese Pearl Milk Tea.\nThere’s got to be something special added to the drink.\n\nThis southeastern Asian fusion restaurant is located on the second floor of Eslite Spectrum. You can reach here by the MRT and get off at Zhongshan Station.\n\nTo sum up, the southeastern Asian dishes they have made are absolutely authentic and impressive with great portions.\nThe service is pretty nice and efficient and the prices are moderate.\nOverall, it’s a 9.5 out of 10!\n\nFYI, you scan the QR code to order and the 10% service charge is included in your bill.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
